 "cards": [
  {
   "dot": "cyan",
   "title": "Long, not wide",
   "items": [
    "One row per respondent × variable in cip_answer, so the schema never changes when weekly modules rotate (BT, TF, HX, IN …)",
    "Definitions (question, item, option, field) are per wave: Forsta codes are not stable across waves, so waves are linked by wording through concepts, never by code",
    "Every table is prefixed cip_ (views v_cip_) so nothing collides with other dwh_stg tables"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "emerald",
   "title": "Serving layer — nothing left for the UI",
   "items": [
    "cip_agg_cell: every answer × standard cut (gender, age band, generation, income, region, urbanicity) × cohort, counted once per load; a standard view is one indexed read",
    "cip_tracker_line: the data team's line-by-line rows for each tracker wave, in their column order",
    "cip_search: one FULLTEXT read for the search box; concept trends join cip_concept_map at read time, so confirming a mapping needs no rebuild"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "amber",
   "title": "Indexes",
   "items": [
    "cip_answer (survey_id, field_id, value_code, respondent_id) covering, plus unique (respondent_id, field_id) for upserts; the duplicate ix_answer_field was dropped",
    "cip_agg_cell (survey_id, map_key, cohort_id, dim) and (survey_id, question_id, dim)",
    "cip_survey (load_status, study_type, wave_date) for wave pickers; cip_forsta_survey (load_state, closed_at) for the due list"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "rose",
   "title": "Partitioning — decided by measurement",
   "items": [
    "Applied: logical partitioning by wave. survey_id leads every hot index, a wave loads and verifies as one unit, and reads hit the pre-computed cube instead of raw answers",
    "Not applied: MySQL PARTITION on cip_answer. InnoDB cannot partition a table with foreign keys or a FULLTEXT index, and cip_answer has both. At 14.3 M rows (1.3 GB data + 2.9 GB index), reads already measure 0.25 s P95",
    "Trigger: above 100 M answer rows, PARTITION BY HASH(survey_id), with integrity moved to the loader's verify step and verbatim search to cip_search"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "violet",
   "title": "Privacy",
   "items": [
    "No browser string, link, session, fingerprint or IP is stored; the panel RID only as sha256 respondent_key",
    "The portal connects with a read-only account; only the ETL writes"
   ]
  }
 ]
